//! The `text-box-trim` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property specifies
//! which of the over and under edges of text content to trim from a text element's block container.
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - none: The default value. No space is trimmed from the text.
//! - trim-both: The start (over) and end (under) edges are both trimmed.
//! - trim-end: The end (under) edge is trimmed.
//! - trim-start: The start (over) edge is trimmed.
//!
//! Grammar: none | trim-start | trim-end | trim-both
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-inline-3/#propdef-text-box-trim
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-box-trim
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

